       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\n- **Ordered:** 1600 mg four times daily, which is 6,400 mg/day.\n- **Maximum:** The usual prescription limit for adults is 3,200 mg/day. Single doses are generally capped at 800 mg, and 400\u2013800 mg every 6\u20138 hours is typical.\n- **Risk:** This is double the daily maximum. It carries a high risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nWas this a typo or a unit error? Here are some common options:\n- **800 mg orally three times daily** (2,400 mg/day), or four times daily (3,200 mg/day, the maximum).\n- **400 mg orally every 6 hours** (1,600 mg/day), which is a common analgesic dose.\n- **1600 mg/day total,** if that was the intended daily amount. It could be split, for example as 400 mg four times daily.\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it right away. If you do want 1600 mg four times daily, please confirm that and give a clinical rationale. I can add the rationale to the order note, though I'd still recommend checking with pharmacy first."
      }
